+// The name of the player before the first game on a server: the Steam version has no such window (Steam gives the
+// name), the player setup of mainui asks for one when the name is a default one ("Player", "unnamed"...). Made in the
+// style of the small windows of the Steam version (as DialogServerPassword.res): 320 x 168, the question (wrapped) at
+// (20, 38), the name at (20, 92) 280 x 24 (the name of the user of the computer at first, as mainui does), OK (the
+// default) and Cancel 72 x 24 at the bottom right. A name mainui doesn't take keeps the window open with a warning;
+// Cancel (or Escape) closes the window that asked too: a game on a server needs a name
+class CSteamPlayerNameDialog : public CSteamFrame
+{
+public:
+	typedef CSteamFrame BaseClass;
+
+	CSteamPlayerNameDialog() : BaseClass( "CSteamPlayerNameDialog", 320, 168 )
