+// New Game, as resource/NewGameDialog.res of Half-Life (the same numbers are built in): the window 372 x 260, the help
+// (dull, wrapped) at (44, 48) 292 x 40, the radio buttons Training Room, Easy, Medium, Hard at (40, 94 + 24 * n)
+// 220 x 24, Play (the default) at (204, 222) and Cancel at (286, 222), 72 x 24.
+// Measured on a screenshot of the Steam version at 1920x1080: the circle of a radio button 14 pixels from (3, 4) of
+// the button, inset (dark above and on the left), the dot of the chosen one 7 pixels wide in "BrightBaseText", the
+// text from 26 pixels, "BrightControlText" for the chosen one; the chosen button in a dotted frame from (3, 3), 19 tall.
+// Play does what the New Game menu of mainui does: Training Room starts the training map ("hazardcourse"), the others
+// a new game with the skill 1, 2 or 3.
+
+#include <string.h>
